  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social Protection, Resilience, Inclusion and Joint Initiatives for Vulnerable People in Need (SPRIJIN) in Moldova (BRC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will improve the wellbeing, resilience and social inclusion of vulnerable people affected by displacement and socio-economic pressures in Moldova, including Ukrainian refugees, older people, people with disabilities and vulnerable host community members. Through community-based mental health and psychosocial support services, individuals will receive emotional support, strengthen coping mechanisms and improve social connectedness. The project will also strengthen the capacity of local volunteers, social service providers and community organisations to identify and respond to protection and wellbeing needs. In addition, the project will support learning and collaboration between humanitarian and social protection actors to promote more inclusive and sustainable support systems. By strengthening both services and local capacity, the project will contribute to improved resilience and wellbeing for vulnerable populations and support longer-term community recovery and social cohesion.</narrative>
  </description>
